        "That was another rebellion of hers.",
        "She started eating.",
        "Not much, but enough.",
        "By evening the first draft of the complaint had been drawn up. Chloe read it word for word. Sometimes she cries. Sometimes she becomes unusually quiet. Sometimes she asked for certain details to be removed and then asked to be added back. Diana never urged her from beginning to end. Arthur left the hard drive containing the evidence and returned to the office. Victim advocate Maya made two follow-up calls.",
        "At half past six, Chloe's old cell phone on the kitchen counter started vibrating like crazy.",
        "It's Julian.",
        "All three of us were glued to the screen.",
        "That name lights up, then goes dark, lights up, then goes dark again, as if he can force reality to give him a response through this forced repetition.",
        "Then there's Victoria.",
        "Then came Beatrice.",
        "Then there's Julian again.",
        "Diana said, \"Don't answer.\"",
        "Chloe whispered, \"He'll be angrier.\"",
        "\"He's already angry.\"",
        "\"He'll find him.\"",
        "\"Then he'll meet that patrol car parked two houses away,\" I said.",
        "She looked at me.",
        "I shrugged. \"Detective Reyes suggested it.\"",
        "The phone vibrated again.",
        "A text message pops up.",
        "Chloe, your mother is brainwashing you. Go home immediately before things become irreversible.",
        "Then there was another one.",
        "I love you. Don't let outsiders destroy us.",
        "Another one.",
        "You have no idea what you are doing.",
        "The last one.",
