        "\"It's not much of a victory,\" she said.",
        "I told her the truth.",
        "\"Indeed. The real victory would be when you raise a son who doesn't need a court injunction to act like a human being.\"",
        "Her eyes were so sinister that she seemed to want to kill someone.",
        "To all of our surprise, Chloe spoke.",
        "\"Don't ever contact me again, Victoria.\"",
        "Victoria turned to her and immediately put on her injured disguise.",
        "\"Chloe, honey—\"",
        "\"Shut up.\"",
        "Two words.",
        "The simplest border.",
        "It is also the hardest boundary.",
        "Victoria opened her mouth, but Diana took a step forward.",
        "\"This prohibition also applies to indirect contact. I advise you to be careful with temptations.\"",
        "We walked right over.",
        "Outside the door, flashes of light flooded in.",
        "Questions came flying like cannonballs.",
        "\"Chloe, are you going to divorce Julian?\"",
        "\"Mrs. Sterling, do his family know about this?\"",
        "\"Eleanor, was it you who leaked the video?\"",
        "\"Is Sterling Industries involved?\"",
        "Chloe froze at the deafening din.",
        "I just wanted to protect her behind me, but she raised her head.",
        "\"My name is Chloe Valentine,\" she said.",
        "All the cameras instinctively went silent.",
        "She said nothing else.",
        "She didn't owe them any more explanations.",
        "But these words have traveled further than any statement written by a public relations person.",
        "By sunset, the words were overwhelming.",
        "My name is Chloe Valentine.",
        "Three days later, Beatrice came to my house.",
        "She didn't say hello in advance and drove a red convertible that was too eye-catching for this quiet street. She parked the car haphazardly, sat in the car for nearly five minutes, and then walked toward the porch with a cardboard box in her arms. Even though it was cloudy, she wore sunglasses.",
        "I looked at her through the curtains.",
        "Chloe was upstairs talking to Maya on the phone.",
        "I opened the door before Beatrice knocked.",
        "She took off her sunglasses.",
        "For the first time since I'd known her, she didn't have that contemptuous smile on her face.",
        "\"Mrs. Valentine.\"",
        "\"What are you here for?\"",
        "She glanced at the patrol car parked on the corner. \"I'm not here for Julian.\"",
        "\"That doesn't answer my question.\"",
        "She slightly raised the cardboard box in her hand. \"Here are some of Chloe's things. Clothes. A picture frame. Her sketchbook. I thought she might want it.\"",
        "\"Julian sent you?\"",
        "\"No.\"",
        "\"Victoria?\"",
        "Beatrice's lips tightened. \"Absolutely not.\"",
        "I looked her over.",
        "Beatrice Sterling had always regarded Chloe as a cheap accessory picked up by Julian during his sentimental phase. She has the kind of fragile beauty unique to wealthy families, with high cheekbones and eyes full of judgment. At dinner parties, she joked about Chloe's meager salary at the nonprofit and the thrift store furniture. At one point, I even heard her call my daughter “Cinderella with a graduate degree.”",
        "And now, she's standing on my porch, looking like someone with severe insomnia.",
        "\"You leaked the video.\" I said.",
        "## Chapter 10",
        "Her expression changed.",
        "Not a denial. It's fear.",
        "I pushed the door open wider.",
        "\"Come in.\"",
        "Her walk into my living room was like walking through an enemy minefield.",
        "I took the cardboard box from her hand and put it on the coffee table.",
        "\"Sit down.\"",
        "\"I'd rather stand.\"",
        "\"As you wish.\"",
        "She sat down.",
        "I'm still standing.",
        "\"Why?\" I asked.",
