        "## Chapter 2: The Call That Changed the Room",
        "The bedroom was quiet for several seconds, with only the faint hum of the air conditioner and the gentle breathing of Ethan's mother on the phone receiver.",
        "Ethan looked at me as if he were a complete stranger.",
        "Maybe he was indeed looking at a stranger.",
        "Maybe the woman he thought he was marrying—the daughter grieving over the loss of her father, the docile fiancée, the bride who accepted every sneer and swallowed every unkind accusation—never really existed. That's just a part of me, but it's not the whole truth. Not even close.",
        "His hand holding the phone tightened.",
        "\"Mom,\" he lowered his voice, \"she's recording.\"",
        "The phone was hung up.",
        "That tiny sound of hanging up sounded harsher than a belt hitting a desk lamp. Harsher than his laugh when he saw me wearing boxing gloves. It was even more deafening than the warnings deep inside me that I chose to ignore because I longed to be loved.",
        "Ethan slowly put down his phone.",
        "\"You have no idea what you just did,\" he said.",
        "I glanced at my phone screen. The recording has been saved successfully. Emergency calls have also been put through. Somewhere, someone is listening right now. Somewhere along the way, our tiny bedroom no longer became the safe haven he thought it was.",
        "\"I know exactly what I'm doing,\" I said.",
        "His face changed between countless emotions: anger, panic, calculation, and finally turned into an almost wounded pride.",
