        "\"But he asked me for my password.\"",
        "\"Did you give it?\"",
        "My silence became the best answer.",
        "Naomi's voice softened half a degree: \"Change it now. Change it all.\"",
        "In the next two hours, I frantically changed my password, turned on security verification, called the bank, and sent emails to the property management company. It was only at this moment that I realized how many pieces of my life Ethan had quietly persuaded me to put into his hands.",
        "He hasn't stolen anything yet.",
        "That's what the bank manager said.",
        "Not yet.",
        "This word accompanies every phone call I make like a ghost.",
        "By early afternoon, exhaustion was weighing on me like wet wool. I was sitting in Aunt Lena's guest room with my laptop open in front of me, papers and cold tea scattered around me. The wedding ring on the ring finger is heavy. I turned it around, then took it off and placed it on the bedside table.",
        "A pale mark was left on the skin.",
        "Aunt Lena knocked lightly on the door.",
        "\"Naomi is here.\"",
