        "\"After your mother died,\" she said, \"your father changed. Not in a way that everyone could see. He went to work as usual, paid his utility bills on time, and made you your favorite pancakes on Sundays as before. But he became wary, withdrawn, and no longer trusted everyone around him.\"",
        "I thought about that version of my father. The man who checked the door lock twice. The man who deliberately took a detour home. The man who taught me to always look for the emergency exit first in a restaurant, taught me how to break free from a wrist lock, but never taught me how to put on mascara.",
        "\"I thought it was just sadness,\" I said.",
