        "## Chapter 6: The Garden Before the Trial",
        "The legal battle continued on and off for nearly two years.",
        "Vanessa faces charges including intentional injury, witness intimidation, destruction of evidence, and conspiracy to commit financial fraud.",
        "Of course, not all the disgusting things she does can be directly turned into criminal charges.",
        "For example, Patricia's request to search my bag was, at best, prejudicial arrogance.",
        "Before the actual stolen goods are found or a consent to theft is reached, a few sentences alone do not meet the most serious felony standards.",
        "George's vicious and vitriolic remarks did not rise to independent charges.",
        "The law punishes specific behaviors that can be corroborated by a chain of evidence.",
        "In court, Vanessa's defense lawyer persisted in trying to characterize my \"incognito private visit\" as entrapment.",
        "Her lawyer cross-examined me:",
        "\"Did you pretend to be poor on purpose?\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"You expect my client to believe that you have nothing to do with the Carter family?\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"You made secret recordings?\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"You told her she would face the consequences?\"",
        "\"That was after she sprayed me with a hose and verbally threatened staff.\"",
        "\"You're setting up a moral test.\"",
        "\"I'm just making an objective observation.\"",
        "\"Her consent was not sought.\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"So, the whole incident was entirely directed by you.\"",
        "\"My clothes were disguises. But her choice to spray me with a garden hose was her choice.\"",
        "The lawyer showed me a candid photo of me on my knees.",
        "\"You could have revealed your identity on the spot.\"",
        "\"Indeed I can.\"",
        "\"But you continued recording anyway.\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"Because you want more damaging evidence.\"",
        "\"Because those employees who have complained about her have the right to know whether she will restrain herself when faced with doubts.\"",
        "\"Do you feel happy when you see her ruined?\"",
        "\"No.\"",
        "This defense not only failed to exonerate Vanessa, but exposed her arrogance of self-esteem.",
        "Luis testified.",
        "He described the moment when he walked over with a napkin in hand.",
        "\"Did Vanessa have the power to fire you at that time?\" the prosecutor asked.",
        "\"I thought she had.\"",
        "\"Why?\"",
        "\"Because she's the future wife of that high-flying activities director.\"",
        "\"Does this affect your behavior?\"",
        "\"Yes.\"",
        "\"What did you do then?\"",
        "\"I took a step back.\"",
        "\"Why are you willing to stand up and testify afterward?\"",
        "\"Because Mrs. Carter recorded the whole process, I know clearly that if I don't come forward, I will definitely end up being one-sided words of their group of wealthy people.\"",
        "The several-minute voicemail was released in court.",
        "\"Before you choose to side with a strange old woman who tells lies, think carefully about your own future.\"",
        "Vanessa's lawyer argued that she was just reminding Luis not to spread false rumors.",
        "Luis replied coldly:",
        "\"Before she even understood what I heard, she had already used her job as a threat to attack me.\"",
        "Samuel's case became the last straw for Mitchell Development Company.",
        "Experts used drawings and objects in court to restore the jerry-rigged bracket, the tampered invoice, and the missing on-site photos.",
        "The prosecutor did not insist that Vanessa personally directed the procurement to cut corners.",
        "Evidence shows that George made the final decision in the purchasing process.",
        "The public relations response was handled by Patricia.",
        "Vanessa was responsible for concocting the online blame-blaming rhetoric for work-related injuries and assisting in the forgery of documents presented to Carter executives.",
        "The jury ruled independently on each man's role.",
        "Vanessa was found guilty of intentional injury, intimidation, perverting justice and financial conspiracy.",
        "Because the prosecutor failed to conclusively prove that she directly received the stolen money from the false invoices, she was not guilty of one of the theft charges.",
        "George was convicted of major fraud, concealing safety hazards and obstruction of justice.",
        "Patricia was found guilty of conspiracy, falsifying records and pressuring witnesses, but the charges were dismissed due to a lack of direct evidence that she personally purchased a poor-quality stent.",
        "The law is about ironclad evidence, not emotional catharsis.",
        "When the verdict was read out in court, Vanessa cried bitterly and defended: \"I was just reacting appropriately to a stranger who broke into the house.\"",
        "And my victim statement only has one sentence:",
        "\"The reason why you sprayed me with a water hose is not because I concealed my identity, but because you were sure that the identity under my clothes could not do anything to you.\"",
        "George downplayed the company's systemic fraud as \"little accounting mistakes.\"",
        "Patricia insists she is \"protecting the family business.\"",
        "Luis's voice message ruthlessly tore off their hypocritical masks and exposed their ugly attitude of treating human life as trivial to the sun.",
        "The verdict came out: imprisonment, full restitution, asset forfeiture, and a lifetime ban from engaging in any trust or business fiduciary management work.",
        "No one applauded in the courtroom.",
        "Ethan did not appear in court.",
        "He said the court should not become a grandstand for another family drama.",
        "But he submitted a written statement publicly acknowledging that it was his long-term connivance and blind trust that made Vanessa's threats ring true and oppressive.",
        "As for myself, I received a formal letter of admonishment from the board of directors after undergoing an independent compliance review.",
